ing-relaxed mb-4">File names follow the same principle. <code class=3D"bg-g=
ray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">standing-desk-home-office.webp</code> =
gives Google useful context before it even looks at the image. <code class=
=3D"bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">IMG_4872.webp</code> gives it =
nothing.</p><p class=3D"text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Use hyp=
hens, not underscores. Google treats hyphens as word separators and undersc=
ores as connectors=E2=80=94<code class=3D"bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded t=
ext-sm">red-office-chair</code> reads as three separate words, <code class=
=3D"bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">red_office_chair</code> reads =
as one.</p></div></div></section><section class=3D"w-full bg-white pb-32 mt=
